{#
  Status vocabulary.

  Every capability, stage, evaluator, component, and interface on this site
  carries one of these three states and a link to the evidence for it.

  The mark beside the label is drawn in CSS as a gauge that is full, half, or
  empty, rather than set as a text glyph. Typed marks were rendering at under
  seven pixels, at which a filled disc and a half-filled one are the same
  dot - so the shape channel carried nothing and the word did all the work.
  Drawing it removes the font dependency and holds the distinction at size.

  Status must survive greyscale, forced-colours mode, and a screen reader
  reading only the label, so the word remains the carrier of record.
#}
{% set status_vocabulary = {
  "available": {
    "label": "Available",
    "definition": "Implemented and reachable in the current checkout. Evidence links to the code, route table, or users' guide section that demonstrates it."
  },
  "in-progress": {
    "label": "In progress",
    "definition": "Partly delivered. Some tasks in the roadmap step are complete and some are not; the capability should not be relied upon."
  },
  "planned": {
    "label": "Planned",
    "definition": "Designed but not built. Evidence links to the design document or roadmap task that specifies it."
  }
} %}

{#
  Upstream evidence bases. Every citation on the site resolves through one of
  these, so a repository move is a one-line change.
#}
{% set source_base = "https://github.com/leynos/episodic/blob/main/" %}
{% set docs_base = source_base ~ "docs/" %}
